WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.502
-Welcome back to "Late Night,"
We're here with

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.937
Hillary Rodham Clinton
and Louise Penny.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.772
Louise, I have a question,
you obviously had an expert who

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:10.009
was telling you these are things
that could actually happen.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:13.580
Being a Canadian, were there
times that American politics

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.983
as explained to Hillary to you,
seem beyond comprehension?

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:20.253
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.988
-What?
You know, I have to say, Seth.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.889
And something I'm not sure
whether you all know,

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:26.292
but this is Canadian
Thanksgiving today.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.526
So I want to say
happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:30.929
-Happy Thanksgiving.
-And there's no way

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:33.499
on Canadian Thanksgiving to say
something ungracious

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:36.102
about our wonderful neighbor.
-I mean yeah.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:40.573
-But what I will say about
Canada versus the united States

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.778
is Justin Trudeau.
-Mm-hmm. Yeah. Okay.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:48.147
[ Cheers and applause ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:50.183
-That's my answer to any
political question.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:53.353
-That's your trump card? Okay.
-Sounds like a sequel to me.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:56.422
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:59.158
-Was it -- were there times,
you know, I think this is

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:01.560
a question of anybody writing
fiction that takes place

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.230
in Washington, D.C. these days,
was there time where

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.932
truth has become so strange
that it is hard to write

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.968
a world that is any different,
or even harder to believe,

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.236
than what we're living through
every day?

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:13.706
-Yeah. You know, I think,
you know, Louise is just

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:17.376
an extraordinary writer
and creates characters

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:22.515
and conceives plots that are
so fascinating and draw you in,

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.251
but truly what's been going on
in Washington,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.553
I think beggars the imagination.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:30.823
It's hard to make it up.
-I think, had we written this

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:34.127
Five, six years ago people would
have said, "No, this is insane,

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.095
this is ridiculous.
-yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.164
-Now, actually, even in the
course of writing it,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.801
it has gone essentially from
fiction to nonfiction.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.604
I mean, what Hillary was talking
about, frighteningly enough

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:47.640
a year and a half ago with me,
when we were discussing it

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.177
is now coming true.
-Yeah, because I've always said,

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.280
"Look, we're gonna get out
of Afghanistan at some point.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.517
And, when we do we gotta remain
vigilant,

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.919
because the terrorists
are not going away.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:04.390
And now in addition to the
Taliban and al-Qaeda,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.094
we now have this ISIS branch
there and they have not

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:11.897
given up on attacking us,
our friends, and our allies.

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:15.501
So people have to be
aware of that.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:19.104
And obviously our leaders
and those who have to protect us

00:02:19.104 --> 00:02:20.406
have to pay attention.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:23.376
And we just have to be smart
and try to think ahead

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:26.179
about what they're trying to do
and what they're going to

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.815
aim at next,
in order to protect ourselves.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.783
-I think it was May,
hopefully I'm right here,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.386
where you referred to
Afghanistan as a wicked problem.

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:37.190
And basically you predicted that
When we left this would happen,

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.525
the Taliban would take over.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:40.760
I think everybody
was caught off guard

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.161
maybe by the speed
it was gonna happen.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.629
But if it had happened
in a week,

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:45.298
if it had happened six months,
if it had happened in a year,

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:48.634
it was going to happen.
Do you think then --

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.470
putting aside how we left,
do you think it was

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.140
the right decision to leave?
-You know,

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.909
it's really difficult to answer
that because

00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:00.279
in the former administration
the United States Government

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:04.917
under Trump made an agreement
that actually Trump's

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:08.554
former national security adviser
McMaster said

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:11.124
was a surrender agreement
to get out by May 1st.

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.892
so when the
United States Government

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:16.629
tells an adversary we're leaving
and then the adversary goes

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.265
"Oh, great, let's get ready
for them to leave."

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.567
Let's go to the village and talk
to Seth, the head guy.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.304
And say, "Seth bring home all
your soldiers or you guys

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.006
are gonna be wiped out."
And, "Let's use our money

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.908
from the opium trade to buy
favor and figure out

00:03:29.908 --> 00:03:31.977
how we're gonna take over,
not just the countryside

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:34.213
but go into the cities,
and particularly Kabul."

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:40.286
That's all entrain and the deal
that Trump made with the Taliban

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.422
was, "Okay, you're leaving we
won't kill Americans

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:44.723
because you're going to leave."

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:47.627
And so, when Biden comes in
he's, like, left with

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:52.131
this total fait accompli,
and his decision has to be

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:54.800
either, get out
in a responsible way.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.635
Which was to push the deadline
a little bit,

00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:59.272
or put in more troops because
they're going to attack us

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.907
and we have to
protect ourselves.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:03.643
It was an absolute, you know,
Hobson's choice.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.711
So, getting out
was going to happen

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:09.748
once the Trump agreement
was reached.

00:04:09.748 --> 00:04:12.285
How we get out, how we protect
ourselves going forward,

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:15.221
how we try to help those Afghans
who stood with us

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:19.224
and were taking on enormous risk
and I'm particularly focused on

00:04:19.224 --> 00:04:22.228
all the women who were
in the government,

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.130
they were journalists,
they were in business,

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.633
they were in education
and health care.

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:31.537
Those are the people that I hope
we can continue to try to

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:35.240
assist and as we also
protect ourselves.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.076
It's complicated.
But, yeah.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:42.214
It's something that once
that was decided was entrain.

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:44.983
-I want to finish with one last
question about the book.

00:04:44.983 --> 00:04:46.985
Your husband Bill was here
with James Patterson

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:48.921
and he admitted
that they were writing a book,

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.457
and that you would be a little
competitive about sales.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.092
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.328
Do you share
this competitive nature?

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:58.965
-Oh, certainly not. No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:02.534
-I know it's impossible to ask
Louise on Canadian Thanksgiving.

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:06.339
-Yeah, she's so gracious.
-Justin Trudeau.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.808
-We heard.
-I just wish everyone well.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:13.145
-You wish everyone well.
How very Louise of you.

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:15.281
I want to thank very much
Hillary Rodham Clinton

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.482
and Louise Penny.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:19.052
"A State of Terror"
is available now.

